message.content:
Sure! Below is a minimal, self‑contained example that shows how to create a “card” element that flips (rotates) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy the code into an HTML file and open it in a browser to see it in action.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑to‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
* { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }

/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;            /* Center horizontally */
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  position: relative;
  transform-style: preserve-3d;   /* Needed for 3D children */
  transition: transform 0.6s;     /* Smooth animation */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Front side of the card */
.card .front,
.card .back {
  position: absolute;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;   /* Hide backside when rotated */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  color: #fff;
  border-radius: 10px;
}

/* Styling for front side */
.card .front {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b);
}

/* Styling for back side */
.card .back {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6a11cb, #2575fc);
  transform: rotateY(180deg);    /* Start flipped */
}

/* Hover effect – flip the card */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="front">Front Side</div>
    <div class="back">Back Side</div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| CSS property | Purpose |
|--------------|---------|
| `perspective` | Sets the distance from the viewer to the z‑plane, giving a realistic 3D depth. |
| `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Allows child elements to maintain their 3D position relative to the parent. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transition: transform 0.6s` | Animates the transform property smoothly over 0.6 seconds. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` | Rotates the card 180° around the Y‑axis (horizontal axis). |

### Tweaking the effect

- **Change rotation axis**: Replace `rotateY` with `rotateX` (vertical flip) or `rotateZ` (spin around the Z‑axis).
- **Adjust speed**: Modify the `0.6s` value in the `transition` rule.
- **Add more faces**: You can add a `.left`, `.right`, `.top`, or `.bottom` face and rotate them accordingly.
- **Add shadows**: Use `box-shadow` on the card or its faces for a more realistic look.

Enjoy experimenting with different angles, colors, and content!
